  "metaDescription": "Indonesian Police chief details an illegal surveillance case involving former officials, including allegations against a former police chief.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "National Police Chief Suyudi Ario Seto detailed a five-stage operation involving the illegal surveillance of President Prabowo Subianto.",
    "Four police generals are currently detained in connection with the case, while one senior officer has been placed under house arrest.",
    "Bareskrim investigators have conducted a search of the former police chief's residence, as eight witnesses seek protection from the LPSK."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police are actively investigating an illegal surveillance operation targeting President Prabowo Subianto. During a recent briefing, Police Chief Suyudi Ario Seto outlined the procedural violations and the modus operandi of the operation, which reportedly included verbal orders issued by former National Police Chief Listyo Sigit Prabowo. Allegations suggest that the former police chief acted as the end user for the intercepted intelligence. In response to these findings, law enforcement authorities have initiated significant legal actions, including the detention of four police generals and the placement of Irjen Slamet Uliandi under house arrest. Additionally, the Criminal Investigation Agency (Bareskrim) searched the former police chief's private home. Amidst the ongoing proceedings, eight individuals serving as witnesses have officially requested protection from the Witness and Victim Protection Agency (LPSK) due to the sensitive nature of the investigation.",
